{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "10", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "01", "M": "26", "S": "58"}}, "news": [{"title": "WeWork India leases 1.61 lakh sq ft in Pune; plans \u20b944 crore investment", "para": "WeWork India has entered into a leave and licence agreement for 1.61 lakh sq ft of space in Pune, which will add approximately 2,881 desks to its portfolio. The new capacity is expected to become operational by July 2027.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/commercial/wework-india-leases-1-61-lakh-sq-ft-in-pune-plans-44-crore-investment/134806314?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-228222/134806314.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "commercial"}, {"title": "Pune: PMC cracks down on potable water use at construction sites, pushes developers to only use treated water", "para": "Pune Municipal Corporation has mandated that all construction developers use treated water in lieu of potable water. This directive follows concerns over water scarcity due to reduced rainfall during an El Ni\u00f1o year. Many developers have already adopted this approach and are promoting awareness within their organizations. The civic administration is also monitoring compliance closely and taking action against any violations.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/infrastructure/pune-pmc-cracks-down-on-potable-water-use-at-construction-sites-pushes-developers-to-only-use-treated-water/134805845?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-498166/134805845.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "infrastructure"}, {"title": "Acquire Harnandipuram land only through talks: HC to Ghaziabad development body", "para": "The Allahabad high court affirmed that land for the Harnandipuram township cannot be acquired unlawfully, ensuring legal compliance. Landowners expressed concerns about fair compensation rates amid low circle rates set by authorities. The Ghaziabad Development Authority plans to proceed through mutual negotiation despite earlier moves toward compulsory acquisition. The project aims to develop 521 hectares across several villages with costs shared by the state government.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/acquire-harnandipuram-land-only-through-talks-hc-to-ghaziabad-development-body/134805799?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-109691/134805799.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}